From 4d63dfbddcf4dc3e67513c3b8ecfc88908bec8a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sven Nierlein <Sven.Nierlein@consol.de>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:19:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Run the command file worker in the main event loop

The external command file was previously polled by a forked worker
process that shipped the commands over a socketpair to the main
process. That created a second naemon process indistinguishable from
the daemon in ps output.

Instead, register the command FIFO fd directly with the main process
I/O broker and process the commands there, the same way the query
handler socket is handled. The dedicated worker process, its
socketpair plumbing; the FIFO is kept open and re-registered across restarts.

tests/test-worker: rewrite the command worker lifecycle test to
check I/O broker registration instead of process state.
